.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Since each pair of test files can only account for one case, this means eight total files added for checking for this behavior, which does feel like a lot 😅 So if you feel some of these test cases can be removed, please let me know and I'll be happy to remove them. (Of course, on the other hand if there are important cases to test that I've missed here, I can add those as well!)\n\nI heard @HolonProduction was eventually thinking of updating the runner so multiple completion tests can be done in one file (I guess meaning everything that's supposed to have the same output like yours does). But for now you can add as many tests as necessary! :D\n\nAnyway, I think the `func _ready():` part is probably necessary since it can also be a member variable, but the tests work either way. I'm just a minimalist, lol.\n\nI don't believe any more tests are necessary since most class enums work the same as each other anyway.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122772#pullrequestreview-5026031040","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122772","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122772#pullrequestreview-5026031040"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122772"}},"submitted_at":"2026-08-26T01:48:46Z","commit_id":"69f55cf383acbc4442bf64f35c4ef18c4056b069"},{"id":5030120754,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK9GNMg","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith